    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d553">

                <pb facs="0869" n="847" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg847"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/12–851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the United States
                        Representative at the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Austin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-10T18:40:00-05:00">December 10,
                            1951—6:40 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Gadel 402. Dept agrees inclusion para on Indians in South Africa quoted in Delga
                    569 on basis it not formal proposal and so not in conflict with position paper
                    recommendations.</p>
                <p> Dept suggests substitution “assistance” for “leadership” in first sentence;
                    deletion “the most” from second sentence; change in penultimate sentence phrase
                    “to preserve their self-respect while they seek” to “in a calm objective
                    atmosphere”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
